    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17119" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτμητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not carved,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				1.322
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.253
				</span></i>
			; <i>uncut,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθειραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.708
				</span></i>
			; <i>unwounded,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				124
			</span></i>; <i>not laid waste, unravaged,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.82
				</span></i>
			: and so metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑγίεια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					6.18
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμπελοι</span>”
				<i>unpruned,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Num.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			; <i>unreaped,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.390
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίβανος ἄ.</span>”
				<i>in lumps,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					PMag.Par.
					1.1991
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργυρεῖα ἄ.</span> silver-mines
				<i>as yet unopened,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Vect.</u>
				4.27
			</span></i>; of animals, <i>entire,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				632a9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>indivisible,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				277b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EE</u>
				1230a29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.505
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>Comm.Math.</u>
				4
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hero
				</span></i>
			<i>*Geom.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				p.85
			</span></i> H. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>that cannot be cut,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				387a6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1023a2
			</span></i>.</div>
